---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Container from '../components/Container.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

const picks = await getCollection('picks');
const paid = picks.filter((p) => p.data.affiliate);
const unpaid = picks.filter((p) => !p.data.affiliate);
---
<Base
  title="How we make money"
  description="Which links pay us, how much that influences what we recommend, and what we refuse to take money for."
>
  <header class="border-b border-line bg-surface-2 py-16 sm:py-24">
    <Container width="prose">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold sm:text-5xl">How we make money</h1>
      <p class="mt-5 text-xl leading-relaxed text-ink">
        Some links on this site earn us a commission when you buy through them. Here is exactly how
        that works, so you can weigh what you read accordingly.
      </p>
    </Container>
  </header>

  <Container width="prose" class="py-14">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        If a product link is paid, it is labelled <strong>Paid link</strong> on the page where it
        appears. Every paid link also carries a <code>rel="sponsored"</code> attribute, which is the
        machine-readable version of the same admission. You never pay more by using one.
      </p>

      <h2>Why the products come last</h2>
      <p>
        Every decision on this site is argued out before a single product is named, and the buying
        section sits at the bottom of the page under a heading that tells you to skip it unless you
        have already made the call. That order is the whole safeguard. A site organised around
        products ends up recommending products, because that is what it has to say.
      </p>
      <p>
        The most common honest answer here is that you do not need to buy anything. A library card,
        a deck of cards and a charger that lives in the kitchen solve more of these problems than
        anything with a price tag.
      </p>

      <h2>What we turn down</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Paid placement. Nobody can buy their way onto a page.</li>
        <li>Sponsored posts and paid reviews, in any form, disclosed or not.</li>
        <li>
          Commission on child monitoring and surveillance software. There is real money in it and it
          conflicts with what we think a trusting household looks like.
        </li>
        <li>Any arrangement that lets a company see or approve what we write before it goes up.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Every product we link, and whether it pays us</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <section class="rounded-2xl border-2 border-line bg-surface-2 p-6">
        <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-extrabold">Paid links ({paid.length})</h3>
        <ul class="mt-3 grid gap-1.5 text-ink-soft">
          {paid.map((p) => <li>{p.data.name}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </section>
      <section class="rounded-2xl border-2 border-line bg-surface-2 p-6">
        <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-extrabold">Earns us nothing ({unpaid.length})</h3>
        <ul class="mt-3 grid gap-1.5 text-ink-soft">
          {unpaid.map((p) => <li>{p.data.name}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-10 text-ink-soft">
      Something look wrong? Write to{' '}
      <a href="mailto:hello@offlinechildhood.com" class="font-semibold text-primary-text underline underline-offset-4">
        hello@offlinechildhood.com
      </a>{' '}
      and we will correct it.
    </p>
  </Container>
</Base>
